IMPORT prelude

-- Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) -- the whole operative Act (ss 2-4), from the seat of the person subject to a
-- restraint of trade.
--
-- SEAT: the person bound by the restraint: an employee or former employee under a non-compete or non-solicitation
-- clause, a person who sold a business and promised not to compete, a member of an association whose rules restrain
-- them. Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Does the Act apply to my restraint?", "How far is my
-- restraint valid?", "Until what day does it bind me?", "Can I go to the Supreme Court?", "What can the Court do?",
-- "From when does its order work?", "Does the order wipe out a claim already made against me?", "Would doing it on this
-- day break my restraint?". The person who imposed the restraint (the employer, the buyer, the association) gets no seat
-- here; the Supreme Court gets none: what it may do is encoded as what it means for the person bound.
--
-- Provisions: s 2 (definitions); s 3 (application); s 4 (validity to the extent not against public policy; the Supreme
-- Court's order; associations; accrued rights). Out: s 1 (name): machinery. What "public policy in respect of restraint
-- of trade" requires is the general law (the common law's reasonableness test): the Act hands it to the court, and the
-- encoding asks the court's view as an input, never deciding it.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a flat "does not apply",
-- a condition introduced by "where", a limit the text sets in its own words), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer
-- on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Forks are numbered as in NOTES.md.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 8 January 2015; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Restraints of Trade Act 1976`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 2(2) "restraint of trade means a restraint of trade created by contract, created by the rules of an association, or
-- otherwise created." s 2(1) "association includes a corporation"; "rules includes memorandum and articles of
-- association of a corporation and provisions of the constitution of an unincorporated association". What a restraint
-- of trade is (a promise or rule restricting someone's freedom to carry on a trade, business or profession) is the
-- general law's term, borrowed: the encoding assumes the person has one. How it was created matters only to s 4(4).
DECLARE `How my restraint was created` IS ONE OF
    `by a contract`
    `by the rules of an association I am a member of`
    `in some other way`

-- s 3(3) the enactments whose operation the Act does not affect.
DECLARE `Another law that deals with my restraint` IS ONE OF
    `no other law`
    `section 304 of the Industrial Relations Act 1996`
    `section 125 of the Co-operatives National Law (NSW)`
    `another enactment about the validity of a restraint of trade`

-- s 2(1) "public policy means public policy in respect of restraint of trade". How much of the restraint is against it
-- is the court's judgment (the general law's reasonableness test), asked as an input.
DECLARE `How much of my restraint is against public policy` IS ONE OF
    `none of it`
    `part of it`
    `all of it`

-- s 4(3): whose manifest failure to attempt to make the restraint reasonable the Court finds; s 4(4) deems an
-- association whose rules restrain a member to have created or joined in creating the restraint.
DECLARE `Whose failure to try to make it reasonable` IS ONE OF
    `a person who created the restraint or joined in creating it`
    `the association whose rules bind me as a member`
    `someone who neither created it nor joined in creating it`
    `nobody: the Court finds no manifest failure`

DECLARE `Does the Act apply to my restraint, and how` IS ONE OF
    `The Act applies to my restraint`
    `The Act applies, and the other law named also operates: the Act does not affect it`
    `The Act does not apply: my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`

DECLARE `How far my restraint is valid` IS ONE OF
    `It is valid: no part of it is against public policy`
    `It is valid only to the extent it is not against public policy (read down), whether or not it is in severable terms`
    `It is not valid: all of it is against public policy`
    `It is invalid for a reason other than public policy, which the Act leaves alone`
    `The Act does not apply: the general law decides`

DECLARE `How long my restraint binds me` IS ONE OF
    `It does not bind me at all`
    `It binds me up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `The Act does not decide this: the general law does`

DECLARE `What the Court may order about my restraint` IS ONE OF
    `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`
    `Only that my restraint is altogether invalid as regards me`
    `That my restraint is altogether invalid, or valid as regards me up to a day no later than` HAS `the latest day` IS A DATE

-- The party and the act of the regulative rule: the restraint itself, as far as the Act leaves it standing.
DECLARE `Restraint party` IS ONE OF `the person subject to the restraint`
DECLARE `Restraint act` IS ONE OF `do what the restraint forbids`

§§ `Day arithmetic`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is earlier than` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `one day` IS A DATE, `another day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `one day` `and` `another day` MEANS
    IF `another day` `is earlier than` `one day` THEN `another day` ELSE `one day`

§§ `s 3 -- does the Act apply`

-- s 3(1) "This Act does not apply to or in respect of a restraint of trade created before the date of assent to this
-- Act." A flat negative. The date of assent is not in the deposited text, so it is asked (finding 1).
-- s 3(2) "This Act applies notwithstanding any stipulation to the contrary": a clause saying the Act does not apply
-- changes nothing (asked, to show it). s 3(3) "This Act does not affect the operation of: (a) section 304 of the
-- Industrial Relations Act 1996, ... (c) section 125 of the Co-operatives National Law (NSW), or (d) any other enactment
-- relating to the validity of a restraint of trade." The Act still applies; the other law runs beside it (fork F1).
@export Does the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) apply to my restraint of trade (for example a non-compete or non-solicitation clause), and does another law also deal with it (ss 2(2), 3)?
GIVEN `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created (for example the contract was signed, or the association's rule was made binding on you) before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `my contract says the Act does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract, or the association's rules, say that the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 does not apply or that you give up its protection
      `another law that deals with it` IS AN `Another law that deals with my restraint` @desc Another law that deals with your restraint. One of: "no other law", "section 304 of the Industrial Relations Act 1996" (the Industrial Relations Commission's power over unfair contracts), "section 125 of the Co-operatives National Law (NSW)", "another enactment about the validity of a restraint of trade"
GIVETH A `Does the Act apply to my restraint, and how`
`Does the Act apply to my restraint` MEANS
    IF `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`
    THEN `The Act does not apply: my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`
    ELSE CONSIDER `another law that deals with it`
         WHEN `no other law` THEN `The Act applies to my restraint`  -- "notwithstanding any stipulation to the contrary" (s 3(2))
         OTHERWISE `The Act applies, and the other law named also operates: the Act does not affect it`

§§ `s 4(1), (2) -- valid to the extent not against public policy`

-- s 4(1) "A restraint of trade is valid to the extent to which it is not against public policy, whether it is in
-- severable terms or not." s 4(2) "Subsection (1) does not affect the invalidity of a restraint of trade by reason of
-- any matter other than public policy." Invalidity for another reason (the contract is void, it was never validly
-- agreed) is the general law's, asked. Severability is asked to show that it changes nothing.
@export How far is my restraint of trade valid under the Act: is it read down to the part that is not against public policy (ss 3(1), 4(1), 4(2))?
GIVEN `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint is invalid for some reason other than being an unreasonable restraint of trade (for example the contract containing it is void, or it was never validly agreed)
      `how much of it is against public policy` IS A `How much of my restraint is against public policy` @desc How much of your restraint a court would find against public policy, that is wider than reasonably needed to protect the other side's legitimate interests (a judgment for the court). One of: "none of it", "part of it", "all of it"
      `my restraint is in severable terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint is written in severable terms (for example a "cascading" clause with alternative periods or areas, or separate promises that can be struck out one by one)
GIVETH A `How far my restraint is valid`
`How far is my restraint valid` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` THEN `The Act does not apply: the general law decides`
           IF `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` THEN `It is invalid for a reason other than public policy, which the Act leaves alone`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `how much of it is against public policy`
               WHEN `none of it` THEN `It is valid: no part of it is against public policy`
               WHEN `part of it` THEN `It is valid only to the extent it is not against public policy (read down), whether or not it is in severable terms`
               WHEN `all of it` THEN `It is not valid: all of it is against public policy`

-- The same, as a period: the restraint is read down to its last day that is not against public policy.
-- "Valid to the extent to which it is not against public policy" (s 4(1)): where the court would allow a shorter period
-- than the one written, the restraint binds for the shorter one. A restraint too wide only in area or activity keeps its
-- period (enter the written last day) and binds only within the part not against public policy.
@export Until what day does my restraint of trade bind me, once the Act reads it down to what is not against public policy (ss 3(1), 4(1), 4(2))?
GIVEN `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint is invalid for some reason other than being an unreasonable restraint of trade
      `how much of it is against public policy` IS A `How much of my restraint is against public policy` @desc How much of your restraint a court would find against public policy (a judgment for the court). One of: "none of it", "part of it", "all of it"
      `the last day the restraint says it binds me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the restraint period as written (for example 12 months after your employment ended)
      `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy` IS A DATE @desc The last day a court would find the restraint could run without being against public policy (a judgment for the court; if only the area or activities are too wide, the same as the written last day)
GIVETH A `How long my restraint binds me`
`Until what day does my restraint bind me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` THEN `The Act does not decide this: the general law does`
           IF `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` THEN `It does not bind me at all`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `how much of it is against public policy`
               WHEN `none of it` THEN `It binds me up to and including` `the last day the restraint says it binds me`
               WHEN `part of it` THEN `It binds me up to and including` (`the earlier of` `the last day the restraint says it binds me` `and` `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy`)
               WHEN `all of it` THEN `It does not bind me at all`

§§ `s 4(3), (4) -- the Supreme Court's order`

-- s 4(3) "Where, on application by a person subject to the restraint, it appears to the Supreme Court that a restraint
-- of trade is, as regards its application to the applicant, against public policy to any extent by reason of, or partly
-- by reason of, a manifest failure by a person who created or joined in creating the restraint to attempt to make the
-- restraint a reasonable restraint, the Court, having regard to the circumstances in which the restraint was created,
-- may, on such terms as the Court thinks fit, order that the restraint be, as regards its application to the applicant,
-- altogether invalid or valid to such extent only (not exceeding the extent to which the restraint is not against public
-- policy) as the Court thinks fit and any such order shall, notwithstanding sub-section (1), have effect on and from such
-- date (not being a date earlier than the date on which the order was made) as is specified in the order."
-- s 4(4) "Where, under the rules of an association, a person who is a member of the association is subject to a
-- restraint of trade, the association shall, for the purposes of subsection (3), be deemed to have created or joined in
-- creating the restraint."
-- s 3(1) A restraint created before assent is outside the whole Act, s 4(3) included.

@export Can I, as a person subject to a restraint of trade, apply to the Supreme Court of NSW for an order under section 4(3) (ss 3(1), 4(3))?
GIVEN `I am subject to the restraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the restraint binds you (you are the person whose trade, business or profession it restricts)
      `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` MEANS
    IF `I am subject to the restraint` AND (NOT `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "on application by a person subject to the restraint" (a "where" condition); s 3(1) flat negative

-- The failure test of s 4(3), with the deeming of s 4(4).
GIVEN `whose failure` IS A `Whose failure to try to make it reasonable`
      `how it was created` IS A `How my restraint was created`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the failure is by a person who created or joined in creating the restraint` `whose failure` `how it was created` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whose failure`
    WHEN `a person who created the restraint or joined in creating it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the association whose rules bind me as a member` THEN
        CONSIDER `how it was created`
        WHEN `by the rules of an association I am a member of` THEN JUST TRUE  -- deemed, s 4(4)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 4(4) deems only for a restraint under the association's rules; whether the association in fact created it is not asked; fork F3)
    WHEN `someone who neither created it nor joined in creating it` THEN JUST FALSE  -- "where": the failure must be by a creator
    WHEN `nobody: the Court finds no manifest failure` THEN JUST FALSE

@export Can the Supreme Court make an order under section 4(3) that my restraint of trade is invalid, or valid only to a lesser extent, as regards me (ss 3(1), 4(3), 4(4))?
GIVEN `I am subject to the restraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the restraint binds you and you are the one applying to the Court
      `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `how my restraint was created` IS A `How my restraint was created` @desc How your restraint was created. One of: "by a contract" (an employment contract, a sale of business agreement), "by the rules of an association I am a member of" (including a corporation's constitution or memorandum and articles), "in some other way"
      `how much of it is against public policy as regards me` IS A `How much of my restraint is against public policy` @desc How much of the restraint, as it applies to you, the Court finds against public policy (a judgment for the Court). One of: "none of it", "part of it", "all of it"
      `whose failure to try to make it reasonable` IS A `Whose failure to try to make it reasonable` @desc Whose manifest (obvious) failure to attempt to make the restraint reasonable the Court finds. One of: "a person who created the restraint or joined in creating it" (for example the employer or buyer who drafted it), "the association whose rules bind me as a member", "someone who neither created it nor joined in creating it", "nobody: the Court finds no manifest failure"
      `the problem is at least partly because of that failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court finds the restraint is against public policy at least partly because of that failure (a judgment for the Court)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` `I am subject to the restraint` `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `how much of it is against public policy as regards me` EQUALS `none of it` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the problem is at least partly because of that failure`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE `the failure is by a person who created or joined in creating the restraint` `whose failure to try to make it reasonable` `how my restraint was created`

@export If the Supreme Court can make a section 4(3) order about my restraint of trade, what may it order: altogether invalid, or valid as regards me up to what latest day (s 4(3))?
GIVEN `I am subject to the restraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the restraint binds you and you are the one applying to the Court
      `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `how my restraint was created` IS A `How my restraint was created` @desc How your restraint was created. One of: "by a contract", "by the rules of an association I am a member of", "in some other way"
      `how much of it is against public policy as regards me` IS A `How much of my restraint is against public policy` @desc How much of the restraint, as it applies to you, the Court finds against public policy. One of: "none of it", "part of it", "all of it"
      `whose failure to try to make it reasonable` IS A `Whose failure to try to make it reasonable` @desc Whose manifest failure to attempt to make the restraint reasonable the Court finds. One of: "a person who created the restraint or joined in creating it", "the association whose rules bind me as a member", "someone who neither created it nor joined in creating it", "nobody: the Court finds no manifest failure"
      `the problem is at least partly because of that failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court finds the restraint is against public policy at least partly because of that failure
      `the last day the restraint says it binds me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the restraint period as written
      `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy` IS A DATE @desc The last day the Court finds the restraint could run without being against public policy (if only the area or activities are too wide, the same as the written last day)
GIVETH A `What the Court may order about my restraint`
`What may the Court order about my restraint` MEANS
    IF `the power` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER `how much of it is against public policy as regards me`
         WHEN `all of it` THEN `Only that my restraint is altogether invalid as regards me`
         OTHERWISE `That my restraint is altogether invalid, or valid as regards me up to a day no later than` (`the earlier of` `the last day the restraint says it binds me` `and` `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy`)
    ELSE `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`  -- from JUST FALSE, and from NOTHING (fork F3): no power the person can rely on
    WHERE
        `the power` MEANS `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` `I am subject to the restraint` `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` `how my restraint was created` `how much of it is against public policy as regards me` `whose failure to try to make it reasonable` `the problem is at least partly because of that failure`

-- "have effect on and from such date (not being a date earlier than the date on which the order was made) as is
-- specified in the order". A date earlier than the order is barred by the text's own words; what an order naming one
-- then does is not said (fork F4).
@export From what day does the Supreme Court's section 4(3) order about my restraint of trade take effect (s 4(3))?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court made the order
      `the day the order says it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the order specifies as the day it takes effect
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From what day does the Court's order take effect` MEANS
    IF `the day the order says it takes effect` `is earlier than` `the day the order was made`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text bars an earlier date but does not say what an order specifying one does; fork F4)
    ELSE JUST `the day the order says it takes effect`

§§ `s 4(5) -- rights accrued before the order`

-- s 4(5) "An order under subsection (3) does not affect any right (including any right to damages) accrued before the date
-- the order takes effect." From the seat: a claim the other side already had against me (for example damages for a
-- breach before that date) survives the order. A right accrued on or after that day is outside s 4(5): the order's own
-- terms decide (NOTHING, a scope limit with no "only").
@export Does the Supreme Court's section 4(3) order take away a right the other side already had against me, such as a claim for damages for an earlier breach of my restraint (s 4(5))?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court made the order
      `the day the order says it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the order specifies as the day it takes effect
      `the day the right accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the other side's right arose (for example the day of the breach they say you committed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `From what day does the Court's order take effect` `the day the order was made` `the day the order says it takes effect`
    WHEN JUST `the day it takes effect` THEN
        IF `the day the right accrued` `is earlier than` `the day it takes effect`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- "does not affect any right ... accrued before"
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 4(5) reaches only rights accrued before; the order's terms decide the rest)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F4)

§§ `The restraint as the Act leaves it -- would doing it on this day break it`

-- The restraint itself is a contractual (or rules-based) prohibition, not a duty the Act creates; the Act decides how far
-- it stands. Written as a rule: from the day the restraint begins (time 0, in days) the person subject to it shall not
-- do what it forbids, up to and including the last day it binds them (WITHIN n counts day n in). Doing it on a later day
-- is not a breach.
GIVEN `the days it binds me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Restraint party` `Restraint act`
`the restraint, as far as the Act leaves it valid, binds the person subject to it` `the days it binds me` MEANS
    PARTY `the person subject to the restraint`
    SHANT `do what the restraint forbids`
    WITHIN `the days it binds me`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person subject to the restraint` BECAUSE "the person did what the restraint forbids on a day it still binds them, within the part that is not against public policy (s 4(1)) or that a section 4(3) order leaves valid"

-- Whether doing it on day D breaks the restraint. Before the day a s 4(3) order takes effect, s 4(1) governs (and s 4(5)
-- keeps any right then accrued); on and from that day the order governs, "notwithstanding sub-section (1)", and cannot
-- leave more valid than s 4(1) does. A restraint invalid for another reason binds on no day (fork F2).
@export Would doing what my restraint of trade forbids, on a given day, break it as the Act (and any Supreme Court order) leaves it (ss 3(1), 4(1), 4(2), 4(3), 4(5))?
GIVEN `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint was created before the Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) received assent in 1976
      `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your restraint is invalid for some reason other than being an unreasonable restraint of trade
      `how much of it is against public policy` IS A `How much of my restraint is against public policy` @desc How much of your restraint a court would find against public policy. One of: "none of it", "part of it", "all of it"
      `the day the restraint begins` IS A DATE @desc The first day the restraint binds you as written (for example the day after your employment ended)
      `the last day the restraint says it binds me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the restraint period as written
      `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy` IS A DATE @desc The last day a court would find the restraint could run without being against public policy (if only the area or activities are too wide, the same as the written last day)
      `what I do falls within the part not against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activity you are asking about (the work, the business, the customers, the area) falls within what a court would find the restraint may reasonably cover
      `the Supreme Court has made a section 4(3) order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has made an order under section 4(3) about your restraint as it applies to you
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court made the order (any day if there is no order)
      `the day the order says it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the order specifies as the day it takes effect (any day if there is no order)
      `the order makes it altogether invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order says the restraint is altogether invalid as regards you
      `the last day the order leaves it valid` IS A DATE @desc The last day the order leaves the restraint valid as regards you (any day if the order makes it altogether invalid or there is no order)
      `what I do falls within what the order leaves valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activity you are asking about falls within what the order leaves valid
      `the day I do it` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or plan to do, what the restraint forbids
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Would doing it on this day break my restraint` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 3(1): the Act does not apply; the general law decides)
           IF `my restraint is invalid for a reason other than public policy` THEN JUST FALSE  -- fork F2
           IF `the day I do it` `is earlier than` `the day the restraint begins` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the Supreme Court has made a section 4(3) order` THEN `with the order`
           OTHERWISE `under section 4(1)`
    WHERE
        `with the order` MEANS
            CONSIDER `From what day does the Court's order take effect` `the day the order was made` `the day the order says it takes effect`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F4)
            WHEN JUST `the day it takes effect` THEN
                IF `the day I do it` `is earlier than` `the day it takes effect`
                THEN `under section 4(1)`  -- s 4(5): before the order takes effect, the restraint as s 4(1) leaves it
                ELSE `under the order`
        `the last section 4(1) day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `how much of it is against public policy` `the last day the restraint says it binds me` `the last day it could bind me without being against public policy`
            WHEN `It binds me up to and including` `the binding day` THEN JUST `the binding day`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        `does it break the restraint up to` `the last binding day` MEANS
            CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the restraint, as far as the Act leaves it valid, binds the person subject to it` (`the days from` `the day the restraint begins` `to` `the last binding day`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person subject to the restraint` `do what the restraint forbids` (`the days from` `the day the restraint begins` `to` `the day I do it`)))
            WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        `under section 4(1)` MEANS
            IF `how much of it is against public policy` EQUALS `part of it` AND (NOT `what I do falls within the part not against public policy`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- valid only "to the extent to which it is not against public policy"
            ELSE CONSIDER `the last section 4(1) day`
                 WHEN JUST `the binding day` THEN `does it break the restraint up to` `the binding day`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE  -- all of it against public policy: it binds on no day
        `under the order` MEANS
            -- "not exceeding the extent to which the restraint is not against public policy": an order cannot widen the
            -- activity or area s 4(1) leaves valid any more than its time (fork F8)
            IF `the order makes it altogether invalid` OR (NOT `what I do falls within what the order leaves valid`)
                OR (`how much of it is against public policy` EQUALS `part of it` AND (NOT `what I do falls within the part not against public policy`))
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE CONSIDER `the last section 4(1) day`
                 WHEN JUST `the binding day` THEN `does it break the restraint up to` (`the earlier of` `the last day the order leaves it valid` `and` `the binding day`)
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE  -- "not exceeding the extent to which the restraint is not against public policy"
